{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 14, :comments ["<b>YHWH will see.</b> Its plain sense is as the Targum renders: YHWH will choose and show Himself this place, to rest His Shekhinah there and to offer sacrifices here." "<b>As is said today.</b> That they will say in the days of the generations about it: On this mountain the Holy One, blessed be He, will be seen by His people." "<b>Today.</b> The days to come — like ״עַד הַיּוֹם הַזֶּה״ throughout Scripture, for all the generations to come who read this verse say ״עַד הַיּוֹם הַזֶּה״ about the day they stand in. And another interpretation: YHWH will see this Binding, to forgive Israel every year and to deliver them from punishment — so that it may be said 'today,' in all the generations to come: On the mountain of YHWH it will be seen — the ashes of Isaac, piled and standing for atonement."], :book :genesis, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 22, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T08:59:59.201056353Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}